# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials are not committed. The one deliberate exception is the bundled GlassOS interop
# material, negated explicitly at the end of this section (see docs/PLAN.md section 2.2). These
# patterns are a backstop, not the mechanism.
*.pem
*.key
# ...but the throwaway test fixture must be committed; it contains generated certs, no secrets.
!apps/spikes/test/fixtures/**
*.p12
*.pfx
certs/
glassos/
# ...but the extracted GlassOS *protocol definitions* are API surface, not secrets, and are the
# whole point of protocol/glassos. Certificates and keys there stay ignored by the *.pem/*.key
# rules above, which is the protection that actually matters.
!protocol/glassos/
!protocol/glassos/**
# Re-assert the credential ban *after* the negation above, because `!protocol/glassos/**` would
# otherwise re-include the very .pem/.key files the rules at the top of this section exist to keep
# out. Verified with `git check-ignore`: protos are committable, credentials are not.
protocol/glassos/**/*.pem
protocol/glassos/**/*.key
protocol/glassos/**/*.p12
protocol/glassos/**/*.pfx
protocol/glassos/**/*.jks
protocol/glassos/**/*.bks
protocol/glassos/**/*.apk

# The one deliberate exception to everything above: the bundled GlassOS interop credentials.
# They are a fixed, shared, already-public keypair (CA `CN=testca`, client `CN=com.ifit.eriador`).
# The material is iFit's own, generated for the console and read back out of its firmware; it is
# already carried inside several distributed apps. Only these three PEM files are reused, never any
# third-party source, so no upstream licence attaches. They unlock a service on hardware the user
# already owns; they guard nothing of the user's and grant no access to any remote account. Committing them is the point, because a tester who has to source their own
# certificates cannot test. Anything a *user* extracts from their own console still lands in
# app-private storage and is still covered by the blanket rules above.
#
# The directory negation must come first: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded by `glassos/`.
!apps/spikes/android/app/src/main/assets/glassos/
!apps/spikes/android/app/src/main/assets/glassos/*.pem

# Captured protocol traces may contain serial numbers and account identifiers. Scrub before
# committing anything under tools/ (docs/PLAN.md section 7).
*.trace
*.pcap
incident-*.log

# Live telemetry captures may contain workout IDs and machine serials.
.telemetry/
